{"name":"Life Is a Peach","hex":"#e5cdbe","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"life","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of organisms preceding their death, characterized by biological processes such as metabolism and reproduction and distinguishing them from inanimate objects; the state of being alive and living.","The status possessed by any of a number of entities, including animals, plants, fungi, bacteria, and sometimes viruses, which have the properties of replication and metabolism."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To replace components whose operational lifetime has expired."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/life"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Life","blocks":[{"text":"Life is the capacity in matter, formed of one or more units called cells, for processes such as cell signalling, homeostasis, metabolism, cell growth, adaptation, response to stimuli, and reproduction. All life eventually reaches a state of death. Many philosophical definitions of living systems have been proposed, such as self-organising systems. Defining life is further complicated by viruses, which replicate only in host cells, and the possibility of extraterrestrial life, which could be very different from life on Earth. Life exists all over the Earth in air, water, and soil, with many ecosystems forming the biosphere. Some of these are harsh environments occupied only by extremophiles. The life in a particular ecosystem is called its biota."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg/330px-Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life","wikidata":"Q3"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach","wikidata":"Q13189"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)","wikidata":"Q5148721"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Male_Lion_and_Cub_Chitwa_South_Africa_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/500px-Male_Lion_and_Cub_Chitwa_South_Africa_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Male_Lion_and_Cub_Chitwa_South_Africa_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/1280px-Male_Lion_and_Cub_Chitwa_South_Africa_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Male_Lion_and_Cub_Chitwa_South_Africa_Lu